// Title: Potential SentinelOne Shell Context Menu Scan Command Tampering
// Sigma ID: 6c304b02-06e6-402d-8be4-d5833cdf8198
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2024-03-06 | Modified: 2026-11-01
// ATT&CK: persistence
// Description: Detects potentially suspicious changes to the SentinelOne context menu scan command by a process
//   other than SentinelOne.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://mrd0x.com/sentinelone-persistence-via-menu-context/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/68e86efccf6969a2175f7e6c280cde81b1ae8eea/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_sentinelone_shell_context_tampering.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\shell\\SentinelOneScan\\command.*$" and (not((((RegistryValueData startswith "C:\\Program Files\\SentinelOne\\Sentinel Agent" or RegistryValueData startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\SentinelOne\\Sentinel Agent") and RegistryValueData contains "\\SentinelScanFromContextMenu.exe") or (InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files\\SentinelOne\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath startswith "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\SentinelOne\\"))))
